  "curriculum": "The 2026–2027 course catalogue verifies a single 180 EC degree with Dutch and English teaching variants of equal academic content. Year one has ten compulsory 6 EC units. Year two has nine compulsory 6 EC units plus one 6 EC choice. Innovation Management in an International Context is selected on academic continuity, with Finance 2 left unselected. Year three reserves 30 EC for a minor, exchange, electives or a 12 EC internship with 18 EC electives, then one 30 EC specialisation. The dated catalogue lists Management in the Digital Age while the current study page calls it The Future of Management and AI. The dated catalogue controls exact course titles and verifies four 6 EC specialisation units and a separate 6 EC thesis and seminar. No other route or alternative component is counted.",
  "progression": "The normal sequence completes 60 EC before year two and 120 EC before year three, satisfying the thesis’s current 90 EC pre-year and 120 EC course-start thresholds. The current course catalogue requires Strategy and Organisation for Innovation Management, Project Entrepreneurship, Strategy and Change and International Management. Marketing precedes Digital Technologies and Marketing, and Organisational Behaviour precedes Management and Leadership in the Digital Age. The first quantitative course precedes the second and the second-year quantitative project. The catalogue’s 10 hours of programme research participation are an additional requirement before passing the thesis, outside the 180 EC. The prior regulations corroborate the normal 48 EC binding-study-advice rule. The proposed year one completes all 60 EC.",
